  "glow_from": "MoveObject's per-type case for object 119, by way of the old port's own table. The client animates the self-luminous submesh alone and not through the model's skeleton: BlendMeshLight scales its brightness and BlendMeshTexCoordV slides its texture, both off the world clock, so every placement of a type moves in step.\n\nThat 'in step' is what makes it cheap — the glow of a type is one material shared by every placement, so it costs one material write a frame however many stand in the town.\n\nAs House04 — the submesh here is a water sheet.",
